"We remember," sang the threads.

Moved by wonder, Memoria blessed all caves and canyons with this gift. From then on, these places became keepers of stories, their walls holding echoes of the past. When people entered and spoke their tales, the stones would remember and whisper them back, ensuring no worthy deed would ever be forgotten.
